   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">08 Oct 2024 | News Release: https://www.adb.org/news/additional-adb-grant-strengthen-energy-security-central-asia</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Grant 0976: 0% of contracts awarded and 0% disbursed as of 04 Feb 2025</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Progress Toward Outcome: Contractors mobilized in 2021. Target deferred from 2021 to 2024. Contract signed in April 2021. Disagreement between TAJ and UZB over the operational regime of the 500kV transmission line L503 has been resolved. The decision over the operational regime of the 500kV transmission line L503 was made during the coordination meeting between TAJ and UZB. the design of the L503 line will not change, and, therefore, the construction of the loop IN/OUT to the Substation Sughd will be carried out according to the TD in the scope of work of the Package 1 Contractor. The mathematical model for the energy system of Tajikistan was completed and handed over to the Employer taking into account the comments of the NDC Republic of Uzbekistan and CDC &quot;Energy&quot; for further actions. Package 2 Contract was signed on 30 March 2021. Overall progress of works is 41%.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Some results are in the Initial Environmental Examination | Jul 2024: https://www.adb.org/sites/default/files/project-documents/52122/52122-002-iee-en_0.pdf</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Some results are in the Resettlement Plans | Jul 2024: https://www.adb.org/sites/default/files/project-documents/52122/52122-002-rp-en.pdf</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: The works progress on the six 220kV interconnection points is as follows:

220kV Regar Denav TL (L-RD): 90%

220kV Regar Zarchob TL (L-RZ): 99%

220kV Sughd Sirdarya TL (L-20S-1): 41%

20kV Sughd Sirdarya TL (L-20S-2): 41%

220kV Sughd Sirdarya TL (L-20US-1): 80%

220kV Sughd Sirdarya TL (L-20US-2): 40%

The works progress on the two 500kV interconnection points is as follows:

500kV Regar Guzar TL (L507): 90%

500kV Regar Surkhan TL (L508): 82%

Target revised from 2022 to 2024. The EPC contractor will train the PMU, in coordination with the PIC. Grant extended until 28 December 2025. Three trainings on emergency control systems and one on relay protection system were conducted for 41 (1 female) BT, SIB and PMUES staff.

The works progress two new interconnection points is as follows:

500kV Sughd Sirdarya TL (L503A): 22%

500kV Sughd Uzbekistanskaya TL (L503B): 22%</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
